### Good Tools to Learn ######################################################

To create and deliver the course we use most or all of the following tools.
You can follow the course without using the command line, but we recommend
learning it if you can; it is debatable that you're ever really in control of
a machine for which your only interface is a GUI (especially when that GUI is
closed source).

It is a good idea to get to know at least Git and if possible the ESP and
Arduino tools before starting (though you should be able to pick them up as we
go along if needed).

- [Git](https://git-scm.com/) and (see above) [GitLab](https://gitlab.com);
  other useful [material
  here](https://git-scm.com/book/en/v2/Git-Basics-Recording-Changes-to-the-Repository)
- [Ubuntu](https://ubuntu.com/) [GNU](https://www.gnu.org/)
  [Linux](https://www.linux.org/) and/or
